{% doc %}
The wording on the guarantee tab: the merchant's shop name, or ours.

The name arrives as an app-data metafield rather than over the app proxy.
This renders in the merchant's theme before any script of ours runs, so a
fetch would mean every page showed "Kourify protection" until it came back.

Interpolated rather than concatenated, because the name does not sit in the
same place in every language: English puts it first, French and Arabic put
it second. A shop that has set no name falls through to the wording the tab
has always used, so nothing changes for it.

Outputs unescaped. The value is the merchant's own text, so every caller
escapes it once at the point it lands in the page.
{% enddoc %}
{%- liquid
  assign kourify_brand = app.metafields.kourify.brand_name.value | default: '' | strip

  if kourify_brand == blank
    echo 'protection.guarantee' | t
  else
    echo 'protection.guarantee_branded' | t: name: kourify_brand
  endif
-%}
